            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to escape, then the Malayalam for to get stuck."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഇര",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇര — ira — \"a victim; prey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തട്ടിപ്പിന്റെ ഇരകൾ പോലീസിൽ പരാതി കൊടുത്തു. taṭṭippinṟe irakaḷ pōlīsil parāti koṭuttu. The victims of the fraud complained to the police."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ഇരകൾ, irakaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First the prey of an animal; in the news, a victim."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇര (ira) is native Dravidian: DEDR 490 lists Malayalam ira, \"food of birds, snakes\", beside Tamil irai, \"prey\". The news uses it for a person something bad happened to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
