          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മൃതദേഹം — mṛtadēhaṁ — \"a dead body\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നാട്ടുകാർ പുഴയുടെ തീരത്ത് ഒരു മൃതദേഹം കണ്ടു. nāṭṭukār puḻayuṭe tīrattŭ oru mṛtadēhaṁ kaṇṭu. The locals saw a dead body on the river bank."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The respectful news word for a body; the plain old word is ശവം."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മൃതദേഹം (mṛtadēhaṁ) is built from two Sanskrit words, mṛta, \"dead\", and deha, \"the body\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
